Subject: [PATCH 5/6] P15C Wave 2 (b): the fact adapter, the ref resolver and
 the replay (1361-E3 r1)

1359-A section 3 and section 10 item 6, commit (b), with 1359-F
Amendment 1 and 1359-F2's F1 ruling:
- src/core/campaignLegacy.ts: legacyFactsFromState(state, boundaryWeek),
  the pure adapter of 1359-A sections 3.1 and 3.2. It passes facts
  through and the law cuts. It reads the three sibling roots untyped
  (1361-F ruling 18): powerRanking's records with their own ids,
  sharedMarket's assessments and corporateCondition's events, by
  p15DomainSequence and week; a sibling root that is absent or recorded
  from the boundary or later reads notRecorded.
- legacyRefResolver, the ref resolver 1359-A section 7 asks Wave 2 to
  export (1361-F ruling 19): one id map per citable root, each ref
  resolving to its position and effective week.
- validateCampaignLegacy gains the checks that read other roots: item 6
  (each source's recordedFromWeek re-derived, a P15 watermark equal to
  the largest sequence below the official's, an array watermark within
  its root's length) and item 7 (every ref through the resolver), then
  the replay under the evaluator the stored definition names, every field
  but standingAtBoundary equal (1359-F Amendment 1).
- The law: an authored film may carry a null settledWeek, and only an
  authored film (1359-F2 F1); ranking facts are unique on (recordId,
  studioId), one row per studio in a record (1359-F3). No outcome moves,
  so the definition stays v2.
- index.ts: exports legacyRefResolver and its two types.

No tick calls the adapter yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
